{"schema_version":"baseline-1.0","run_kind":"single_agent_baseline","sequence":2,"event_id":"evt-0e7eb1ff-df42-41f9-893d-f8c517c885bd","run_id":"baseline-dc690467-3088-4e23-820b-1c694fc055d8","actor":{"kind":"runtime"},"occurred_at":"2026-11-02T02:25:16.600008200+00:00","prev_hash":"044a5e30807bde693ae2b3de0700347423042ea71365f05a4019574493201ae6","hash":"de27965246e23df0acfb55804a56ab712a88cf466bc89467bfc668d1565ce611","payload":{"type":"recall_planned","plan":{"source":{"kind":"consensus_log","log_sha256":"faaf46b9e506f90f53217ef9eac189f68b13af7ffe4c9afe81bc3e8a23fad6ee","run_id":"run-aa966e9f-db00-455d-bc04-8f714d8839ad"},"queries":["This proposal does not increase retry attempts, expand retryable operations, or change retry backoff relative to the existing documented retry constraints.","This proposal adds no retries for payment requests; mitigation is limited to connection-pool/keep-alive configuration and explicit connect/read timeout configuration.","Any retry occurring after this change will follow the pre-existing documented retry-eligibility rules, including any documented idempotency requirement.","The revised configuration sets the payment-client RetryPolicy to max_attempts=3 and jitter_ms=50, replacing the default max_attempts=1 and jitter_ms=0 and staying within the documented cap of 3 attempts with at least 50 ms jitter.","send_with_retries will retry only SendError::Timeout up to RetryPolicy.max_attempts; upstream errors will be returned at once without a retry.","Verification will run constraint_cap_is_three_attempts, which fails when max_attempts is above 3 or jitter_ms equals 0.","constraint_cap_is_three_attempts fails when max_attempts is above 3 or jitter_ms equals 0; it does not by itself enforce the documented minimum of 50 ms, so verification will separately assert that the configured jitter_ms is at least 50."],"limit_per_query":5,"max_records":20}}}
